      "writtenOn": "2018-06-08T14:42:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The register bit controlled by the GPIO_INPUT flag doesn\u0027t matter when you set the alternate mode (nor should it since it is no longer muxed to be a GPIO pin).\n\nWhen in i2c alternate mode, this pin is an input and output so saying input is misleading.\n\nThe default gpio pin configuration for I2C7_SCL uses GPIO_INPUT to\n 1) put the pin in Hi-Z state before the the alternate mode takes it over\n 2) prevents the `gpioset` command from working on the EC console (b/c the alternate should be controlling it)\n\nAlso, when we put the gpio pin into raw_gpio mode [0] to try to unwedge the bus, we configure the pin to be open-drain output.\n\nI have also tested this without the GPIO_INPUT flag and it works well.\n\n\n[0] https://chromium.git.corp.google.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/7c294e0f7b1163d055f95a27f6f344bb525cb010/common/i2c_master.c#390",
